{{!-- A1, "centered classic": cover photo, centred titling, one column at the measure with the
contents list above the article.

There is no grid here. The design source wraps both layouts in the same one-or-two-column
grid, and with a single `minmax(0,1fr)` track a centred `measure` child sits exactly where a
plain block puts it — so the wrapper would be a box that does nothing. A2 has the grid because
A2 has the second column. --}}
{{> "post/hero"}}

<div class="container pt-14">
	<div class="measure mx-auto min-w-0">
		{{!-- The contents list goes when the article goes; post/rail.hbs carries the reasoning for
		both layouts, which hang the same list in different places. --}}
		{{#if access}}
			{{> "post/toc" variant="inline"}}
		{{/if}}

		{{> "post/body"}}

		{{> "post/share"}}

		{{> "post/end-blocks" detail=true}}
	</div>
</div>
